        <schema:discussionUrl>https://nemoanalytics.org/index.html?layout_id=1b58cf00&amp;gene_symbol=gad2&amp;gene_symbol_exact_match=1</schema:discussionUrl>
        <schema:headline>CCN202002013</schema:headline>
        <schema:includedInDataCatalog rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pcl/CCN202002013"/>
        <schema:position>MOp</schema:position>
        <rdfs:comment>10x 3&apos; v2 is the second version of the 10x sequencing technology that sequences from the 3&apos; end of nucleic acid molecules. In the 3&apos; assay, the polyd(T) sequence is part of the gel bead oligo (which also contains the 10x barcode, UMI, and partial Illuma Read 1 sequence), with the template switch oligo (TSO) supplied in the RT Primer.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Mouse MOp (CCN202002013) single nuclei 10x Chromium v2</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>10x Chromium v2</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012458 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012458">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://schema.org/Dataset"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000028>Mouse MOp snmC-Seq2</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:PCL_0010061 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9941</obo:PCL_0010061>
        <schema:archivedAt>https://data.nemoarchive.org/biccn/grant/u19_cemba/cemba/epigenome/sncell/ATACseq/mouse/processed/analysis/EckerRen_Mouse_MOp_methylation_ATAC/</schema:archivedAt>
        <schema:assesses>mouse</schema:assesses>
        <schema:discussionUrl>https://brainome.ucsd.edu/annoj/BICCN_MOp/index.html?location=6:7555070:100:1&amp;ensemble=2&amp;celltype=inh&amp;colorby=modality&amp;groupby=celltype&amp;modalities=mcg:atac:scrna:snrna:enhancer</schema:discussionUrl>
        <schema:headline>CCN202002013</schema:headline>
        <schema:includedInDataCatalog rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pcl/CCN202002013"/>
        <schema:position>MOp</schema:position>
        <rdfs:comment>A single-nucleus sequencing assay (library preparation method) that involves fragmentation of genomic DNA followed by adapter ligation, bisulfite conversion and limited amplification using adapter-specific PCR primers in preparation for sequencing. This enables the genome-wide indentification of cytosine DNA methylation states at single-base resolution.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Mouse MOp (CCN202002013) single nuclei snmC-Seq2</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>snmC-Seq2</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012459 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012459">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://schema.org/Dataset"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000028>Mouse MOp snATAC-Seq</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:PCL_0010061 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">813799</obo:PCL_0010061>
        <schema:archivedAt>https://data.nemoarchive.org/biccn/grant/u19_cemba/cemba/epigenome/sncell/ATACseq/mouse/processed/analysis/EckerRen_Mouse_MOp_methylation_ATAC/</schema:archivedAt>
        <schema:assesses>mouse</schema:assesses>
        <schema:discussionUrl>https://brainome.ucsd.edu/annoj/BICCN_MOp/index.html?location=6:7555070:100:1&amp;ensemble=2&amp;celltype=inh&amp;colorby=modality&amp;groupby=celltype&amp;modalities=mcg:atac:scrna:snrna:enhancer</schema:discussionUrl>
        <schema:headline>CCN202002013</schema:headline>
        <schema:includedInDataCatalog rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pcl/CCN202002013"/>
        <schema:position>MOp</schema:position>
        <rdfs:comment>Assay for transposase-accesibble chromatin using sequencing (ATAC-seq) is a method based on direct in vitro transposition of sequencing adaptors into native chromatin and is a rapid and sensitive method for integrative epigenomic analysis. ATAC-seq captures open chromatin sites using a simple two-step protocol.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Mouse MOp (CCN202002013) single nuclei snATAC-Seq</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>snATAC-Seq</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012460 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012460">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://schema.org/Dataset"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000028>Mouse MOp MERFISH</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:PCL_0010060 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">300000</obo:PCL_0010060>
        <schema:archivedAt>https://download.brainimagelibrary.org/biccn/zeng/zhuang/merfish/M1/</schema:archivedAt>
        <schema:assesses>mouse</schema:assesses>
        <schema:discussionUrl>https://nemoanalytics.org/index.html?layout_id=7e14ad94&amp;gene_symbol=gad2&amp;gene_symbol_exact_match=1</schema:discussionUrl>
        <schema:headline>CCN202002013</schema:headline>
        <schema:includedInDataCatalog rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pcl/CCN202002013"/>
        <schema:position>MOp</schema:position>
        <rdfs:comment>An imaging assay that measures the copy number and spatial distribution of hundreds to thousands of RNA species in single cells.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Mouse MOp (CCN202002013) MERFISH</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>MERFISH</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012461 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PCL_0012461">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://schema.org/Dataset"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000028>Mouse MOp scPatch-seq</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:PCL_0010060 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1237</obo:PCL_0010060>
        <schema:archivedAt>https://knowledge.brain-map.org/data/FTX8VQ3E93P26HK79V3/summary</schema:archivedAt>
        <schema:assesses>mouse</schema:assesses>
        <schema:discussionUrl>https://nemoanalytics.org/index.html?layout_id=c4416938&amp;gene_symbol=gad2&amp;gene_symbol_exact_match=1</schema:discussionUrl>
        <schema:headline>CCN202002013</schema:headline>
        <schema:includedInDataCatalog rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pcl/CCN202002013"/>
        <schema:position>MOp</schema:position>
        <rdfs:comment>A sequencing assay wherein a patch clamp recording is taken from a neuron and then scRNA sequencing is performed on the cell soma. During recording, the cell is also filled with biocytin dye enabling imaging and reconstruction of cellular morphology.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Mouse MOp (CCN202002013) single cell Patch-seq</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>Patch-seq</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


