        <rdfs:comment>In Human primary motor cortex (CCN201912131), Inh L1-2 VIP WNT4 is a member of the Sncg subclass. The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is LOC105379064 and SYT9 (F-beta = 0.453), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. Inh L1-2 VIP WNT4 cells represent 5.81% of all Sncg cells collected in the Human M1 10Xv3 dataset. Inh L1-2 VIP WNT4 cells have an average of 6143 genes detected, which is 1889 more than the average for all Sncg cells (4254).</rdfs:comment>
