        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GABAergic</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>GABAergic is: Neurons that use GABA as a neurotransmitter and which exert an inhibitory post-synaptic effect. The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is GAD1 (F-beta = 0.97), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. GABAergic cells represent 31.31% of all cells collected in the Human M1 10Xv3 dataset. GABAergic cells have an average of 4678 genes detected, which is 789 less than the average for all cells (5467).</rdfs:comment>
