        <rdfs:comment>In Human primary motor cortex (CCN201912131), Inh L1 LAMP5 NMBR is a member of the Lamp5 subclass. The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is PCDH18 and RELN (F-beta = 0.639), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. Inh L1 LAMP5 NMBR cells represent 4.33% of all Lamp5 cells collected in the Human M1 10Xv3 dataset. Inh L1 LAMP5 NMBR cells have an average of 4036 genes detected, which is 722 less than the average for all Lamp5 cells (4758).</rdfs:comment>
