        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Non-Neuronal</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Non-Neuronal is: Non-neuronal cells of neuroectoderm origin (sometimes called glia). The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is ST18 (F-beta = 0.919), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. Non-Neuronal cells represent 5.07% of all cells collected in the Human M1 10Xv3 dataset. Non-Neuronal cells have an average of 2119 genes detected, which is 3348 less than the average for all cells (5467).</rdfs:comment>
