        <rdfs:comment>In Human primary motor cortex (CCN201912131), Inh L3-5 VIP HS3ST3A1 is a member of the Vip subclass. The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is ABI3BP and IQGAP2 and SLC22A3 (F-beta = 0.624), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. Inh L3-5 VIP HS3ST3A1 cells represent 4.63% of all Vip cells collected in the Human M1 10Xv3 dataset. Inh L3-5 VIP HS3ST3A1 cells have an average of 4150 genes detected, which is 98 less than the average for all Vip cells (4248).</rdfs:comment>
