        <rdfs:comment>Glutamatergic is: Neurons that use glutamate as a neurotransmitter and exert an excitatory post-synaptic effect. The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is SV2B and ARPP21 (F-beta = 0.952), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. Glutamatergic cells represent 53.63% of all cells collected in the marmoset M1 10Xv3 dataset. Glutamatergic cells have an average of 4405 genes detected, which is 781 more than the average for all cells (3624).</rdfs:comment>
