        <rdfs:comment>In Marmoset primary motor cortex (CCN201912132), Inh GAD1 PCP4 is a member of the Sncg subclass. The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is PATJ and THSD7B (F-beta = 0.524), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. Inh GAD1 PCP4 cells represent 30.73% of all Sncg cells collected in the marmoset M1 10Xv3 dataset. Inh GAD1 PCP4 cells have an average of 3147 genes detected, which is 183 less than the average for all Sncg cells (3330).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>RNAseq 13 - CS201912132_13</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>Inh GAD1 PCP4</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


