        <rdfs:comment>In Mouse primary motor cortex (CCN202002013), L4/5 IT_2 is a member of the L4/5 IT subclass. L4/5 IT_2 includes the Patch-seq and connectivity types L4/5 IT. The minimal set of markers required to distinguish this cell type from other cell types in the primary motor cortex is Col26a1 and Cpne4 and Il1rapl2 (F-beta = 0.707), based on the NS Forest method of marker gene selection. L4/5 IT_2 cells represent 40.86% of all L4/5 IT cells collected in the snRNA-seq 10X v3 B dataset. L4/5 IT_2 cells have an average of 5125 genes detected, which is 449 more than the average for all L4/5 IT cells (4676). L4/5 IT_2 cells have an average firing rate of 23.13 Hz, compared to 26.01 Hz for all L4/5 IT cells recorded. Other distinguishing features include an input resistance of 161.96 MOhms (170.7 MOhms in all L4/5 IT cells), and upstroke:downstroke ratio of 4.5 (4.38 for all L4/5 IT cells). The most distinguishing morpholgical features of L4/5 IT_2, as determined by reconstructions from Patch-seq data, are normalized cortical depth (0.37 vs. 0.34 average for all L4/5 IT cells), dendrite total length (3927.39 vs. 3357.7 microns for all L4/5 IT cells), and stems (7.78 vs. 6.86 for all L4/5 IT cells).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>RNAseq 062 - CS202002013_62</rdfs:label>
